{"text": "i\n\nTHE\nEy Menican Memorandum\n\n[TOBACCO\n\u2018COMPANY\n\n\"pr. Eugene Glock . bw November 11, 1988\nree W. L. Rickett, N. L, Bodenhamer, C. A. Schettino; and R. L, Slater\n\n\u2122 Leaf Services Monthly Report for October\n\nTobacco Expansion\nA, Reidsville FEP Production\n\nThe FET-55 moisture (12.4%), filling power (9.9 ce/g),\n2 mm sieve fraction (70.38) averages for the month of\nOctober fell within an acceptable range. The FET-0S\nfilling power (10.0 cc/g) and 2 ma sieve fraction\n(66.28) monthly averages are within an acceptable range,\nbut the moisture average (11.5%) is below the desired\n12-13% range. \u2018The operation of the R-1l recovery system\nin October (R~11 utilization ratio 0.21) was slightly\nbetter than that of September (ratio 0.23). Rell recovery\nshould continue to improve as the sources of air leaks are\ndiscovered and corrected, and when the best operating\nparameters are established.\n\nThe FET Quality Improvement Team met twice during October.\nAt one of the meetings a progress report was presented\nto the Reidsville Plant Steering Committee. This report\nwas summarized in a memorandum to Dr. P. H. Leake dated\nOctober 10, 1988.\n\nB, Alternate Methods of Expansion\n\nLarge quantities (600 pounds of each) of R-123 and R-141b\nhave been ordered from DuPont and Pennwalt, respectively,\nfor use in expansion experiments.\n\nC. Service to other Departments\n\nAs a service to the Blend Development Group, several sam-\nples of blended tobacco that had been through the nicotine\nreduction treatment were dried in the vertical steam flash\ndryer using the parameters shown in Table I. The levels\nof R-1l and filling power after drying were measured and\nare reported in Table I. Other details can be found in\nNotebook A272 cn pages 190-194. \u2018The nicotine reduction\n\nATX02 0009777",
